cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Hindsight dataset, please cite it as below.
  The data in data/out is licensed CC BY 4.0 (rows derived from
  data/raw/bcb-focus are ODbL 1.0); the code is MIT licensed.
  See NOTICE.md.
title: "Envisioning Hindsight: published forecasts, graded against what happened"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: Envisioning
    website: "https://www.envisioning.com"
version: "2026.2"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/envisioning/hindsight"
url: "https://www.envisioning.com/hindsight"
abstract: >-
  Hindsight is a public record of published forecasts about the future,
  checked against what happened. Each forecast is a dated claim with a named
  source and a stable id, graded with cited evidence; every change to a grade
  stays in the record. Release 2026.2 holds 28,306 claims from 36 sources
  published between 1976 and 2026.
keywords:
  - forecasting
  - forecast evaluation
  - foresight
  - trend reports
  - dataset
